    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. INPUT & MEDIA PREPROCESSING\n\nThree ways in — **Manual** (demo), **Form** (upload straight from n8n) and\n**Webhook** (called by the React UI at `localhost:47300`).\n\n`Upload Video to Storage` is the **only** node that ever carries binary data.\nFrom there on every node passes just `job_id` and object keys — a 500 MB video\nnever travels through the workflow.\n\n**FFmpeg** extracts a mono 16 kHz WAV, **Demucs** splits it into\n`speech.wav` + `background.wav`.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 1560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "0b752955-2d5a-4b21-a741-9258e932db6f",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. SPEECH UNDERSTANDING\n\n`faster-whisper` → text **with timestamps**\n`pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1` → who spoke when\n\nCommunity-1 is a *complete* pipeline (segmentation + embedding + VBx clustering\nin one checkpoint) and returns an **exclusive** diarization where every instant\nbelongs to at most one speaker — which is what makes reconciling it with\nWhisper's coarser timestamps unambiguous.\n\n`merge` → one document per utterance:\n\n```json\n{ \"segment_id\": 12, \"speaker_id\": \"SPEAKER_01\",\n  \"start\": 10.2, \"end\": 12.7, \"duration\": 2.5,\n  \"source_language\": \"en\", \"source_text\": \"...\" }\n```\n\nIt also cuts a voice-reference wav per speaker for the cloning TTS.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 740,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "9b2e2a21-c829-4f86-95af-9bc4a1f59917",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. MULTILINGUAL TRANSLATION\n\n**NLLB-200** (200 languages) with a per-segment character budget so the\ntranslation *reads* in roughly the same time as the original line.\n\nModel A fails → the error output routes to **SeamlessM4T**. Both converge on\n`Translation Ready`, so a single model outage never kills the run.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "70bf2ceb-f85b-45c7-832a-01c2c0217342",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        960
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. SPEECH GENERATION\n\nRouter, not a single model:\n\n```\nif language_supported_by_voice_clone:\n    XTTS-v2 (clones the original speaker)\nelse:\n    MMS-TTS (language-specific)\n```\n\nEach take is measured:\n`ratio = generated_duration / original_duration`",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "80f380e3-2f0d-4f27-88be-091b49dd4ac3",
      "name": "Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        960
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. TEMPORAL SYNCHRONIZATION\n\n```\n0.90 ≤ ratio ≤ 1.10  → accept\n0.80–0.90 / 1.10–1.20 → light stretch\n< 0.80 or > 1.20      → rewrite + re-voice\n```\n\nThe IF node loops back until every line fits (retries are capped server-side).\n\nTakes are **overlaid at their original `start`** on a silent canvas — never\nconcatenated end to end.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "25d6cba5-dcb0-4f0c-9878-8d9bbb8dc565",
      "name": "Note 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        960
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. AUDIO MIXING & VIDEO RENDERING\n\n`dubbed speech + preserved background` → loudness-normalised final mix\n→ `.srt`/`.vtt` → FFmpeg mux onto the untouched video stream.\n\nEvery stage that can fail routes its **error output** to\n`Report Pipeline Failure`, which records the error code in Postgres so the UI\nturns that stage red.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "2b0c3582-2a1c-454e-a61b-27cde6d4e182",
      "name": "Note 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        380,
        960
      ]
    }
